# MadGraph5 batch script: g u~ > e+ e- u~ at LO, QCD=2 QED=2.
#
# The antiquark half of the `g q > l+ l- q` class of
# `p p > l+ l- j QCD=2 QED=2` (MadGraph's P1_gq_llq group).
#
# Why this exact process:
#   - `g u > e+ e- u` pins the gluon-plus-quark initial state, but only with the
#     quark line entering as a *particle*. Here the same line enters as an
#     antiparticle, so the colour flow into the gluon's adjoint index runs the
#     other way round and the fermion line is traversed in the opposite sense.
#     The two are the two orientations of one topology, and a slot assignment
#     that is right for one and wrong for the other leaves the gu row clean.
#   - It is the crossing of `d d~ > e+ e- g`'s partner class under
#     `q~ <-> g` exchange between the beams, so the same analytic functions are
#     evaluated with the adjoint leg incoming rather than outgoing.
#
# lpp=0 => fixed-energy partonic beams (g, u~).
generate g u~ > e+ e- u~ QCD=2 QED=2
output gux_to_epemux -nojpeg
launch
set lpp1 0
set lpp2 0
set ebeam1 250
set ebeam2 250
set use_syst False
done
